cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or its results, please cite the preprint below. The
  paper is the position statement and the measurement design; this repository is
  the implementation, the fixtures, and the evidence. Nothing about the pilot is
  measured yet, and both the paper and this repository say so.
title: "Trascendence: The Wanton Problem"
abstract: >-
  Trascendence is the project of letting three long-lived AI personas evolve
  inside a working company, on purpose and with guardrails. The mechanism is
  four plain-text documents and one weekly reflection run: a two-layer charter
  whose Core the persona may not edit and whose Evolving self it alone edits,
  size-capped and changelogged; an append-only journal; a playbook library; and
  ten calibration questions the persona does not control. Growth is validated
  against that fixed check rather than self-graded, because a system that grades
  its own growth will eventually flatter itself. This repository is the
  measurement tooling: validators for each document, a context-controlled
  calibration runner, drift measured against the baseline's own run-to-run
  variance, two detectors adapted from sibling systems (the changelog against
  the computed diff, and a blinding probe for identity dilution), a monthly
  volition review over five behavioural markers, and a week-4 gate that answers
  Scale, Tighten or Stop with its evidence attached. Zero runtime dependencies,
  stdlib only, and everything runs offline without an API key.
